9 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186053511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055379 #edb/ref 1069 "q-560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055379 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055379 #edb/ref 1071 "$5(8x+3)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055379 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6a0a35d-7b70-51dc-89d3-efb1feb64960" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055379 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(8x+3) & = \\\\ 5\\cdot 8x+5\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ 40x+15\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055793 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055793 #edb/ref 1061 52198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055793 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0260c802-439e-52f2-a68b-09274c6a571b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055793 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055794 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055794 #edb/ref 1061 52199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055794 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2773b7a6-5cf0-5ec7-ab24-7c3f3e071778" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055794 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055795 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055795 #edb/ref 1061 52202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055795 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "13fb6de4-d0af-5464-a0b6-d0869bef3942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055795 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055796 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055796 #edb/ref 1061 52205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055796 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bf71b983-d8a0-5ea7-b63f-9c9cc0dee5ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055796 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055797 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055797 #edb/ref 1061 52206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055797 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b50cc40-2af9-5f98-b18f-05c4449bce2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055797 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055798 #edb/ref 1061 52209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055798 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9c926434-2ec0-590c-b30c-36f58052ba12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055798 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056023 #edb/ref 1064 "The **distributive law** states that multiplying a group of terms by a number is the same as multiplying each term separately by that same number and adding the products.\n\nFor example, let's take a look at the following expression: \n\n$$\n2(3+4).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate this expression using the distributive law:\n\n![](images/4c/4ca32844e45f756ce88e4d8e6d73e8b69099d2c517157b51fed9bb1f02a699ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3+4) & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ 6+8 & = \\\\ 14 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 6+8 & = \\\\ 14 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056023 #edb/ref 1065 8112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056023 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "38c806d3-fe46-5786-81c9-63a1d1bdd9d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056023 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056024 #edb/ref 1064 "The distributive law also works when there is subtraction inside the parentheses. \n\nFor example, we can expand the expression $2(3-4)$ as follows:\n\n![](images/05/05ba4424f566b35af2a279b994c3a8f13564560deaa60f1c7c4616f52d2fb8d6.png)\n\nNotice that we keep a plus ($+$) sign between the two terms. This helps us to avoid mistakes when multiplying with negative numbers.\n\nNow, evaluating our expression, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3-4) & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot (-4) & = \\\\ (6)+(-8) & = \\\\ 6-8 & = \\\\ -2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (6)+(-8) & = \\\\ 6-8 & = \\\\ -2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056024 #edb/ref 1065 8113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056024 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ac1d8340-9788-5072-a2ae-b1a73d0df048" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056024 #edb/ref 1067 "Dealing With a Minus Inside the Parentheses" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445112 #edb/ref 1080 "-40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445112 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445112 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "071411a0-3d13-5b6d-acf3-f829e6765509" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445113 #edb/ref 1080 "40x-15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445113 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445113 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17a71d18-2373-5b34-b0ee-6cee8fb4daac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445114 #edb/ref 1080 "15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445114 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445114 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1eea5216-9dec-522d-8e89-e2a2e3d59f9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445115 #edb/ref 1080 "-40x+15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445115 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445115 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "340a5ab9-11ca-55a1-86ac-9be79f5a7430" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445116 #edb/ref 1080 "40x+15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445116 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445116 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "356915f5-cbce-57bf-8584-53e5840fc46d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445117 #edb/ref 1080 "-7k+14i" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445117 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445117 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37362d40-8c2b-568e-934c